26
00:01:05,223 --> 00:01:05,592
that will

27
00:01:06,586 --> 00:01:08,253
take this selected code

28
00:01:08,911 --> 00:01:11,268
into account or that will take this selected

29
00:01:11,412 --> 00:01:12,262
code as a base.

30
00:01:13,561 --> 00:01:16,944
For example, if I use /explain with this

31
00:01:16,944 --> 00:01:19,702
code selected, I don't need to type anything

32
00:01:19,814 --> 00:01:20,071
else.

33
00:01:20,617 --> 00:01:23,554
I could to add more instructions or more

34
00:01:23,683 --> 00:01:24,405
context,

35
00:01:24,951 --> 00:01:27,343
but I can also run it like this to have this

36
00:01:27,535 --> 00:01:28,033
code

37
00:01:28,643 --> 00:01:29,702
be explained to me.

38
00:01:30,906 --> 00:01:33,089
I could add more information if I wanted to

39
00:01:33,089 --> 00:01:35,449
