66
00:02:41,384 --> 00:02:42,210
use the

67
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:45,690
logging package. And chances are high that

68
00:02:45,690 --> 00:02:47,924
it would've worked as well,

69
00:02:48,506 --> 00:02:49,073
as you can tell.

70
00:02:51,142 --> 00:02:52,401
But by using

71
00:02:52,982 --> 00:02:55,435
/fix, you're adding some extra context

72
00:02:55,435 --> 00:02:55,952
again. And

73
00:02:56,694 --> 00:03:00,262
using these AI chat tools is all about

74
00:03:00,262 --> 00:03:03,159
context. It's always about adding the right

75
00:03:03,159 --> 00:03:05,813
context in the right place because with this

76
00:03:06,477 --> 00:03:08,824
/fix command, we make it very clear that we

77
00:03:08,824 --> 00:03:10,259
wanna fix this code.

78
00:03:11,664 --> 00:03:14,021
And therefore, for certain commands where

79
00:03:14,102 --> 00:03:16,427
sometimes GitHub Copilot might

80
00:03:16,975 --> 00:03:19,704
not always give us the right response, the

81
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:23,192
right result, adding little extra pieces of

82
00:03:23,273 --> 00:03:25,598
context like this can make the difference,

83
00:03:25,695 --> 00:03:27,504
which is why it's important to know about

84
00:03:27,504 --> 00:03:27,552
it.

